{"causes": ["The ongoing development and codification of canon law necessitated skilled jurists like Frédol to organize and interpret complex ecclesiastical decrees.", "The establishment of the Avignon Papacy created a centralized administrative hub where legal experts could directly contribute to papal governance and jurisprudence.", "The need for the papacy to assert and solidify its legislative authority against secular challenges and internal disputes during the 14th century propelled figures like Frédol into prominence."], "effects": ["Bérenger Frédol's legal expertise directly contributed to the compilation and promulgation of the *Clementines* in 1317, solidifying a key part of canon law.", "His work helped to standardize and reinforce papal legislative authority, influencing ecclesiastical legal practice for centuries within the Catholic Church.", "The clarity and organization he brought to papal decrees facilitated the administration of justice and governance across the vast reach of the medieval Church."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "clement-v", "sourceName": "Pope Clement V", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "bérenger-fredoli", "targetName": "Bérenger Fredoli", "context": "Pope Clement V appointed Bérenger Fredoli as a cardinal in 1305 and entrusted him with significant legal and administrative responsibilities during the early Avignon Papacy."}, {"sourceSlug": "bérenger-fredoli", "sourceName": "Bérenger Fredoli", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "clementines", "targetName": "Clementines", "context": "Bérenger Fredoli played a crucial role in the compilation and revision of the *Clementines*, a collection of papal decrees promulgated in 1317."}, {"sourceSlug": "bérenger-fredoli", "sourceName": "Bérenger Fredoli", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "council-of-vienne", "targetName": "Council of Vienne", "context": "Bérenger Fredoli actively participated in the Council of Vienne (1311–1312), contributing to its decrees which were later incorporated into the *Clementines*."}, {"sourceSlug": "bérenger-fredoli", "sourceName": "Bérenger Fredoli", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "avignon-france", "targetName": "Avignon, France", "context": "Bérenger Fredoli spent a significant portion of his career serving the papacy in Avignon, where he contributed to legal and administrative reforms during the Avignon Papacy."}, {"sourceSlug": "corpus-juris-canonici", "sourceName": "Corpus Juris Canonici", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "clementines", "targetName": "Clementines", "context": "The *Clementines*, significantly shaped by Bérenger Fredoli's work, became an integral fifth book of the *Corpus Juris Canonici*, the fundamental legal compilation of the Catholic Church."}], "places": [{"name": "Avignon, France", "role": "Papal Residence & Administrative Center"}, {"name": "Frascati, Papal States", "role": "Cardinal-Bishopric"}, {"name": "Montpellier, France", "role": "Legal Education Center"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Bérenger Fredoli", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "bérenger-fredoli"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q521012", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berengar_Fredol_the_Elder"], "tags": ["France", "Religious Figures", "Europe", "comparative-religion", "doctrine-development", "cultural-diffusion"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Bérenger Fredoli's direct involvement in compiling the *Clementines* profoundly influenced the codification and application of canon law, solidifying papal authority and shaping ecclesiastical governance for centuries across Europe.", "significanceCategory": "continental"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-27T13:11:59Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30269005368", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Berengar Fredol or Bérenger Frédol was a French canon lawyer and Cardinal-Bishop of Frascati.", "newValue": "Bérenger Frédol the Elder (d. 1323), a distinguished French canon lawyer and Cardinal-Bishop of Frascati, played a pivotal role in shaping papal jurisprudence during the tumultuous Avignon Papacy. Born in the late 13th century in the diocese of Béziers, he rose through ecclesiastical ranks, becoming a key intellectual and administrative force within the Curia. His career spanned the reigns of several popes, most notably Clement V and John XXII, for whom he served as a trusted advisor and legal expert, contributing significantly to the consolidation of papal authority and the codification of canon law.

Frédol's most enduring contribution was his involvement in the compilation and revision of the *Clementines*, a collection of papal decrees issued by Clement V and later promulgated by John XXII in 1317. This collection, which included decrees from the Council of Vienne (1311–1312) and other papal constitutions, aimed to clarify and update the existing body of canon law. As a skilled jurist, Frédol's expertise was crucial in organizing these complex legal texts, ensuring their coherence and enforceability across the Catholic world. His work on the *Clementines* solidified his reputation as one of the preeminent legal minds of his era, directly influencing the administration of justice within the Church.

The *Clementines*, largely shaped by Frédol's legal acumen, became an integral part of the *Corpus Juris Canonici*, the foundational legal text of the Catholic Church, remaining in force for centuries. His efforts helped to standardize ecclesiastical legal practice and reinforced the Pope's legislative supremacy at a time when papal authority faced challenges from secular rulers and internal dissent. Frédol's legacy thus extends beyond his lifetime, as his contributions to canon law continued to inform legal scholarship and ecclesiastical governance, influencing generations of jurists and shaping the institutional structure of the Church."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-27T13:11:59Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30269005368", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1250, France"}, {"title": "Spiritual seeking and religious community formation", "type": "Idea", "year": "1250, France"}], "newValue": ["The ongoing development and codification of canon law necessitated skilled jurists like Frédol to organize and interpret complex ecclesiastical decrees.", "The establishment of the Avignon Papacy created a centralized administrative hub where legal experts could directly contribute to papal governance and jurisprudence.", "The need for the papacy to assert and solidify its legislative authority against secular challenges and internal disputes during the 14th century propelled figures like Frédol into prominence."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-27T13:11:59Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30269005368", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Shaped religious practice and spiritual communities", "type": "Idea", "year": "1323-06-19"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1323-06-19"}], "newValue": ["Bérenger 